__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*_BACKUP_contaminated*

# Large regeneratable binary data caches -- pooled z-score windows, FIR
# design matrices, trial tables (tens to hundreds of MB each, sometimes
# multi-GB; outputs_fixed/ alone is ~39GB on disk). These are reproducible
# from raw session data via each analysis's own prep script + a recorded
# manifest.json (git commit + parameters), so git tracks the small,
# diffable summary of a run (CSVs, JSON, small pickles) rather than the
# regeneratable data itself. Figures are equally regeneratable from that
# same tracked code + data and are excluded for the same reason.
*.npz
*.parquet
*.png
*.svg
